@startuml 02a-component-toolchain
!include ../_style.iuml
title CMU Sphinx reference: toolchain components and their contracts

package "SphinxTrain (acoustic model trainer)" {
  component "Perl orchestration\nscripts/NN.step/slave_*.pl\n(00.verify ... 90.deleted_interpolation,\ndecode/slave.pl)" as PERL
  component "SphinxTrain::Config\nSphinxTrain::Util\n(Log, RunTool, RunScript,\nLaunchScript, WaitFor*)" as STLIB
  component "Queue, Queue::POSIX,\nQueue::PBS, Queue::Job" as Q
  component "C tools (bin/)\nbw, norm, init_mixw, mk_mdef_gen,\nmk_flat, bldtree, prunetree, tiestate,\ninc_comp, map_adapt, sphinx3_align,\nmk_s2sendump, sphinx_fe ..." as CT
  component "Python modules\ncmusphinx.lda, cmusphinx.mllt\n(numpy, scipy)" as PY
  component "scripts/sphinxtrain\n(Python CLI: setup / run / -s step)" as STCLI
}
package "PocketSphinx (decoder)" {
  component "pocketsphinx_batch" as PSB
  component "libpocketsphinx\n(acoustic scoring, search:\nfwdtree, fwdflat, bestpath)" as LIBPS
  component "pocketsphinx_lm_convert" as LMC
}
package "CMU-Cambridge SLM Toolkit (language model)" {
  component "text2wfreq -> wfreq2vocab ->\ntext2idngram -> idngram2lm" as SLM
}
package "Scoring" {
  component "word_align.pl\n(DEC_CFG_ALIGN=builtin)" as WA
}

interface "etc/sphinx_train.cfg\n(Perl: $CFG_*, $DEC_CFG_*)" as CFG
interface "etc/feat.params\n(-lowerf -upperf -nfilt -feat -cmn ...)" as FP
interface "etc/<db>_*.fileids / .transcription\n<db>.dic  <db>.filler  <db>.phone" as LISTS
interface "*.mfc feature files" as MFC
interface "model_parameters/<db>.cd_cont_<N>/\nmdef means variances mixture_weights\ntransition_matrices feat.params" as AM
interface "ARPA / DMP / BIN LM" as LM

STCLI --> PERL : runs steps in order
PERL --> STLIB
STLIB --> Q : LaunchScript -> submit_job
PERL --> CT : RunTool
PERL --> PY : 01/02 via python
PERL ..> CFG : require
PERL ..> LISTS
CT ..> FP
CT ..> MFC : bw reads features
CT ..> AM : writes
PERL --> PSB : decode/psdecode.pl
PSB --> LIBPS
PSB ..> AM
PSB ..> LM
PSB ..> MFC
PERL --> WA : compute_acc
SLM ..> LM : writes .arpa
LMC ..> LM

note bottom of Q
  Parallelism lives here. CFG_NPART training slices and DEC_CFG_NPART
  decode slices become Queue jobs. Default CFG_QUEUE_TYPE is "Queue"
  (run inline, serial); "Queue::POSIX" forks locally;
  "Queue::PBS" submits each job with qsub. No Slurm backend exists upstream.
end note
@enduml
